<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Achieng was asked to list <m>C = {\{x : x \text{ is an integer}, -4 &lt; x &lt; 3\}}</m>. Achieng wrote <m>C = {\{-4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2\}}</m>.</p><p>(a) What is wrong with the list?</p><p/><ol marker="(1)">
<li>It includes an end value that the rule leaves out.</li>
<li>It leaves out an end value that the rule includes.</li>
<li>It includes 1, which is not a prime number.</li>
<li>It includes 0, which is not a natural number.</li>
<li>Nothing: the list is correct.</li>
</ol>  <p>(b) Write the correct list.</p><p><fillin characters="25" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Test each element of Achieng's list, and each end value, against the rule <m>C = {\{x : x \text{ is an integer}, -4 &lt; x &lt; 3\}}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>-4</m> is an end value, and the rule leaves it out, so it must not be listed.</p><p>(b) The correct list is <m>C = {\{-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2\}}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>(1)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{-3 , -2 , -1 , 0 , 1 , 2 \right \}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>